    - id: 4
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: Manual Commissary
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: "<div class=\"section-header\">SECTION 4 \uFFFD OFFENDER TRUST ACCOUNTS
          / FUNDS</div>\n\n<div class=\"institutional\">\nPRISONER FUNDS \uFFFD 4.01\n\nAll
          prisoner funds are maintained by the State by \nmeans of computerized accounting.
          Funds may be \nreceived through the U.S. mail at any time. Funds \nmay
          also be deposited at the facility by immediate \nfamily members Monday
          through Friday, 8:00 a.m. \nto 4:00 p.m.\n\nCOMMISSARY \uFFFD 4.03\n\nYou
          must have sufficient funds in your account on \nthe day you order commissary.
          The money will be \ndeducted the same day.\n\nCommissary purchase limit
          for Phase I prisoners \nis [var=25].00 per week.\n\nPhase I prisoners include:
          newly remanded prisoners, \npretrial detainees, and those serving less
          than \none year.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"warning\">\nINDIGENT ORDERS \uFFFD
          4.04\n\nAn indigent prisoner is one who has less than [var=20].00 \npresently
          available on their account and who has had \nno more than [var=50].00 in
          their account during the \npreceding 30 days. Indigent status is determined
          by \ncomputer and will be reflected on your prisoner \naccount statement.\n\nIndigent
          orders for five envelopes per week, writing \npaper, pencil, toothpaste,
          toothbrush, cup, comb, \nshampoo, and soap are to be filled at the same
          time \non the Indigent Commissary Form.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"player-thought\">\nYou
          do the math on the indigent section. \nLess than [var=20] available. No
          more than [var=50] in \nthe last 30 days.\nYou're not sure what's in your
          account right now. \nYou're not sure how to find out.\nThere's a form for
          the indigent supplies. \nYou'd need to submit a cop-out to get it.\nA cop-out
          requires a form you also don't have yet.\n</div>\n\n---"
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 15
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: Block
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 15
        originDialogueID: 4
        destinationConversationID: 15
